{
  "kind": "Dashboard",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "thalamus_debug_llm_d",
    "project": "workload-management"
  },
  "spec": {
    "display": {
      "name": "Thalamus Debug LLM-d"
    },
    "variables": [
      {
        "kind": "TextVariable",
        "spec": {
          "display": {
            "name": "Rate Interval",
            "hidden": false
          },
          "value": "15m",
          "name": "rate_interval"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "TextVariable",
        "spec": {
          "display": {
            "name": "Rate Multiplier (per-second \u2192 per-hour = 3600)",
            "hidden": false
          },
          "value": "1",
          "name": "rate_multiplier"
        }
      }
    ],
    "panels": {
      "readme": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "display": {
            "name": "README"
          },
          "plugin": {
            "kind": "Markdown",
            "spec": {
              "text": "# Thalamus Debug LLM-d\n\n## Description\n\nDiagnostic metrics from the llm-d endpoint picker / router (EPP). When the SLO dashboard shows a breach, this dashboard explains whether the router, scheduling, or prefix-routing layer is contributing. Everything here is from EPP's perspective \u2014 the model-server view lives in Debug/vLLM.\n\nHistograms of latencies are split into **p50** and **p99**. Token-count histograms are wrapped in `round()` because token counts are inherently integer; latency, ratio, and byte histograms are left as-is.\n\n## Why some panels used to show only `http-metrics`\n\nPrometheus attaches an `endpoint` label to every scraped series \u2014 it is the **scrape endpoint name** from the ServiceMonitor/PodMonitor (the port is named `http-metrics`), not an EPP routing endpoint. Several EPP metrics do not carry a direct `model_name`/`target_model_name` label, so the dashboard must derive the model from `job` or use the model-specific labels that do exist.\n\n## Variables\n\n- `$rate_interval` (default `15m`) \u2014 histogram/counter smoothing window.\n- `$rate_multiplier` (default `1`) \u2014 1 = per-second, 3600 = per-hour.\n\n## Sections\n\n### Queue & Routing\n\n#### Average Queue Size\nPool-average queued request count across endpoints, grouped by model (`name` label).\n\nQuery: `sum by (name) (llm_d_epp_average_queue_size)`\n\n**Debug scenario:** `llm_d_epp_average_queue_size` climbs while `vllm:num_requests_waiting` stays flat \u2192 EPP is queuing requests before they reach vLLM. Check `Per-Endpoint Queue Size` for imbalance.\n\n#### Per-Endpoint Queue Size\nQueue depth per actual vLLM endpoint (`model_server_endpoint` label).\n\nQuery: `sum by (model_server_endpoint) (llm_d_epp_per_endpoint_queue_size)`\n\n**Debug scenario:** Endpoint A has queue=50, B and C have queue=0 \u2192 prefix-aware routing or another affinity plugin is pinning traffic to one endpoint.\n\n#### Scheduler E2E Duration p50 / p99\nTime EPP takes to pick an endpoint. Adds directly to user-visible latency before the request reaches vLLM. Model name is derived from the `job` label because the metric lacks a model label.\n\nQuery: `histogram_quantile(0.50|0.99, sum by (model, le) (label_replace(rate(llm_d_epp_scheduler_e2e_duration_seconds_bucket[$rate_interval]), \"model\", \"$1\", \"job\", \"(vllm-.*)-epp\")))`\n\n**Debug scenario:** SLO E2E p99 spikes but vLLM E2E p99 is flat. Scheduler E2E p99 here is 400ms \u2192 the router itself is slow. Check `Plugin Duration` to find the culprit plugin.\n\n#### Scheduler Attempts\nScheduling outcomes by `status` and `target_model_name`.\n\nQuery: `sum by (status, target_model_name) (rate(llm_d_epp_scheduler_attempts_total[$rate_interval])) * $rate_multiplier`\n\n**Debug scenario:** `status=\"error\"` rate rises \u2192 EPP cannot find a valid endpoint, possibly because health checks are failing even though pods appear ready.\n\n#### Plugin Duration p50 / p99\nLatency per routing plugin, grouped by model (derived from `job`) and `plugin_name`.\n\nQuery: `histogram_quantile(0.50|0.99, sum by (model, plugin_name, le) (label_replace(rate(llm_d_epp_plugin_duration_seconds_bucket[$rate_interval]), \"model\", \"$1\", \"job\", \"(vllm-.*)-epp\")))`\n\n**Debug scenario:** Scheduler E2E is high. Plugin `prefix-aware` p99 is 200ms \u2192 that plugin is slow. Disable or cache it.\n\n### Prefix Indexer\n\nPrefix-indexer metrics do not expose `name`, `model_name`, or `target_model_name`. The model is derived from the `job` label.\n\n#### Prefix Indexer Size\nNumber of entries in EPP's prefix index, grouped by model.\n\nQuery: `sum by (model) (label_replace(llm_d_epp_prefix_indexer_size, \"model\", \"$1\", \"job\", \"(vllm-.*)-epp\"))`\n\n**Debug scenario:** Size grows without bound \u2192 prefix index is leaking entries. Memory pressure on the EPP pod will follow.\n\n#### Prefix Indexer Hit Ratio p50 / p99\nHit ratio of EPP prefix-aware routing, grouped by model.\n\nQuery: `histogram_quantile(0.50|0.99, sum by (model, le) (label_replace(rate(llm_d_epp_prefix_indexer_hit_ratio_bucket[$rate_interval]), \"model\", \"$1\", \"job\", \"(vllm-.*)-epp\")))`\n\n**Debug scenario:** Low hit ratio despite repeated system prompts \u2192 the prefix index is cold, or the prefix is too short to match the configured block size.\n\n#### Prefix Indexer Hit Bytes p50 / p99\nBytes of prefix matched per routing decision, grouped by model.\n\nQuery: `histogram_quantile(0.50|0.99, sum by (model, le) (label_replace(rate(llm_d_epp_prefix_indexer_hit_bytes_bucket[$rate_interval]), \"model\", \"$1\", \"job\", \"(vllm-.*)-epp\")))`\n\n**Debug scenario:** Non-zero confirms prefix-aware routing is active; correlate with TTFT to confirm latency benefit.\n\n### Latency Cross-checks\n\n#### nTPOT p50 / p99\nConcurrency-normalized TPOT. Backs out GPU timeslicing so you can tell whether the model itself is slow.\n\nQuery: `histogram_quantile(0.50|0.99, sum by (target_model_name, le) (rate(llm_d_epp_request_ntpot_seconds_bucket[$rate_interval])))`\n\n**Debug scenario:** vLLM TPOT p99 = 4s but nTPOT p99 = 0.05s \u2192 the model is fast per-user; the perceived latency is from concurrent requests timeslicing the GPU, not a model problem.\n\n#### Non-streaming TTFT p50 / p99\nTTFT for non-streaming requests. For these clients this equals e2e latency, so this panel is a diagnostic cross-check.\n\nQuery: `histogram_quantile(0.50|0.99, sum by (target_model_name, le) (rate(llm_d_epp_request_ttft_seconds_bucket{streaming=\"false\"}[$rate_interval])))`\n\n**Debug scenario:** If non-streaming TTFT diverges from `llm_d_epp_request_duration_seconds`, the internal measurement points have a timing anomaly.\n\n### Payload Sizes\n\n#### Request Size p50 / p99\nIncoming HTTP request body size.\n\nQuery: `histogram_quantile(0.50|0.99, sum by (target_model_name, le) (rate(llm_d_epp_request_size_bytes_bucket[$rate_interval])))`\n\n**Debug scenario:** p99 > 1 MB \u2192 someone is sending huge JSON payloads (for example a base64 image to a text model).\n\n#### Response Size p50 / p99\nOutgoing HTTP response body size.\n\nQuery: `histogram_quantile(0.50|0.99, sum by (target_model_name, le) (rate(llm_d_epp_response_size_bytes_bucket[$rate_interval])))`\n\n**Debug scenario:** Very large responses correlate with high output token counts. Large responses plus streaming add network overhead per request.\n\n### Container & Network\n\n#### Container FS Reads\nFilesystem read rate per model. High rate during startup is normal (weights loading); sustained high during inference means weights are paging from disk.\n\nQuery: `sum by (model) (label_replace(rate(container_fs_reads_bytes_total{container=\"vllm\"}[$rate_interval]), \"model\", \"$1\", \"pod\", \"(vllm-.+)-[a-z0-9]{10}-[a-z0-9]{5}$\")) * $rate_multiplier`\n\n#### Container Network Receive Errors\nNetwork receive errors per vLLM pod.\n\nQuery: `sum by (pod) (rate(container_network_receive_errors_total{namespace=\"thalamus\", container=\"vllm\"}[$rate_interval])) * $rate_multiplier`\n\n**Debug scenario:** Non-zero \u2192 packet corruption or CNI issue on this pod. Check node NIC and CNI logs.\n"
            }
          },
          "queries": []
        }
      },
      "avg_queue_size": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "display": {
            "name": "Average Queue Size"
          },
          "plugin": {
            "kind": "TimeSeriesChart",
            "spec": {
              "legend": {
                "mode": "list",
                "position": "bottom"
              },
              "visual": {
                "areaOpacity": 0.3,
                "connectNulls": false,
                "display": "line",
                "lineStyle": "solid",
                "lineWidth": 1.5,
                "pointRadius": 2
              },
              "yAxis": {
                "format": {
                  "unit": "decimal"
                },
                "min": 0,
                "show": true,
                "label": "count"
              }
            }
          },
          "queries": [
            {
              "kind": "TimeSeriesQuery",
              "spec": {
                "plugin": {
                  "kind": "PrometheusTimeSeriesQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "datasource": {
                      "kind": "PrometheusDatasource",
                      "name": "kube-monitoring-prometheus"
                    },
                    "query": "sum by (name) (llm_d_epp_average_queue_size)",
                    "seriesNameFormat": "{{name}}"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
